[34:20m2026-07-07 20:02:29,470 - iac-eval - INFO - Model raw output: **Description of the Terraform Program:**

This Terraform configuration sets up a reverse DNS (PTR) record in Amazon Route 53. It creates a private hosted zone named "reverse_zone" and adds a pointer (PTR) record for the domain "host.example53.com". This configuration assumes that the domain is associated with an IP address that is part of a VPC, as Route 53 private hosted zones are used for internal DNS resolution within a VPC.

---

**Terraform HCL Program:**

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_route53_zone" "reverse_zone" {
  name = "reverse_zone"
  type = "private"
  vpc {
    vpc_id      = "vpc-12345678" # Replace with your actual VPC ID
    private_zone = true
  }
}

resource "aws_route53_record" "ptr_record" {
  zone_id = aws_route53_zone.reverse_zone.id
  name    = "host.example53.com"
  type    = "PTR"
  records = ["192.168.1.100"] # Replace with the actual IP address
  ttl     = 300
}
```

---

**Notes:**

- Replace `"vpc-12345678"` with the actual VPC ID where the private hosted zone should be associated.
- Replace `"192.168.1.100"` with the actual IP address for which the reverse DNS record is being created.
- This configuration assumes that the IP address is part of a private network and that the VPC is correctly configured to support private hosted zones in Route 53. (eval.py:730)[0m
