This Terraform configuration will create an AWS Lightsail instance with a MySQL database. It will configure daily backups to occur between 16:00 and 16:30 each day. Additionally, it will set up maintenance windows for any changes that could cause an outage (such as attribute changes) to occur only on Tuesdays between 17:00 and 17:30. The configuration includes a provider block for AWS, a Lightsail instance, a MySQL database, and the necessary backup and maintenance settings.

---

```hcl
provider "aws" {
  region = "us-east-1"
}

resource "aws_lightsail_instance" "mysql_instance" {
  name              = "mysql-instance"
  availability_zone = "us-east-1a"
  blueprint_id      = "mysql80"
  bundle_id         = "mysql80-standard"
  tags = {
    Name = "mysql-instance"
  }
}

resource "aws_lightsail_database" "mysql_db" {
  name              = "mysql-db"
  engine            = "mysql"
  engine_version    = "8.0"
  instance_type     = "db.t3.medium"
  master_username   = "admin"
  master_password   = "SecurePassword123!"
  allocated_disk    = 20
  backup_retention  = 7
  daily_backup_time = "16:00"
  maintenance_window = "tue:17:00"
  tags = {
    Name = "mysql-db"
  }
}
```

---

This configuration assumes the use of the `aws_lightsail_database` resource, which is available in the `hashicorp/aws` provider version 5.75 and above. The `daily_backup_time` is set to 16:00, and the `maintenance_window` is set to `tue:17:00`, which aligns with your requirements. The `master_password` is set with a default value, but you should replace it with a secure password in production. (eval.py:730)[0m
